#: ../../../sound/codecs/tas675x.rst:794
msgid "Clock Fault Behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/codecs/tas675x.rst:797
msgid "On Stream Stop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/codecs/tas675x.rst:799
msgid ""
"Every time a playback stream stops the FAULT pin briefly asserts. The ASoC "
"PCM trigger stop sequence calls DAIs in reverse order, so the CPU DAI stops "
"SCLK before the codec can transition to sleep. The device detects the clock "
"halt and latches ``CLK_FAULT_LATCHED``, which asserts the FAULT pin. The "
"driver clears the latch in the ``mute_stream`` callback that follows, so the "
"FAULT pin flicker lasts only a few milliseconds. Audio output is not "
"affected and no kernel log message is produced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/codecs/tas675x.rst:809
msgid "On Rapid Rate Switching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/codecs/tas675x.rst:811
msgid ""
"When streams are started in rapid succession, an intermittent ``Clock Fault "
"Latched: 0x01`` message may appear in the kernel log. A (conservative) ~0.5 "
"second gap between sessions eliminates this."
msgstr ""

